propsSchema.description:
Runs one GET /h3/query against an indexed H3 dataset, lands the Parquet result in DuckDB and exposes it as a named SQL source. Any SQL widget in reach of this node (the same node, or one connected by an edge) references the result via {{name}}; children are rendered as given. Every string or number prop accepts a $param reference ("$lat") or inline text ("$year-01-01"); the query waits until every referenced parameter has a value and re-runs when one changes. At most one spatial selector: cell, lat+lng, the four bounding box edges, or hexMin+hexMax; none reads the whole dataset.

## Example

```json
{
  "type": "h3-query",
  "props": {
    "name": "nyc311",
    "path": "s3://fused-asset/data/nyc311/",
    "minLng": -73.99, "minLat": 40.75, "maxLng": -73.98, "maxLat": 40.76,
    "timeMin": "$date_min", "timeMax": "$date_max",
    "columns": ["hex", "created_date", "complaint_type"]
  },
  "children": [
    { "type": "sql-table", "props": { "sql": "SELECT complaint_type, COUNT(*) AS calls FROM {{nyc311}} GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10" } }
  ]
}
```
